 "phrases": [
  "Wait. That's a myth. Microwaves don't cook food from the inside out.",
  "Let's look inside.",
  "This tube is the magnetron. It fires invisible waves.",
  "The same kind of waves as your Wi-Fi. Just way more powerful.",
  "They bounce off the metal walls, again and again.",
  "Now zoom into the soup. Into a single drop of water.",
  "Water molecules are lopsided. One side slightly positive, the other slightly negative.",
  "The waves flip about two and a half billion times a second. Each time, the molecules spin to follow.",
  "All that spinning and bumping? That's heat.",
  "But the waves only reach the outer layer. The center heats later, from the outside in.",
  "And they don't spread evenly. That's why the plate spins, and why you should stir.",
  "Last thing. The holes in the door are smaller than the waves. Light gets out. Microwaves don't.",
  "Ding. Now stir it before you eat.",
  "Pop quiz: why does frozen food heat so unevenly? Comment below.",
  "Follow Tech Unseen. Next lesson: how does GPS know exactly where you are?"
